This licence covers the files in this folder except media/: everb.asm,
generate.py, manifest.py, verify.py, perf.py, octamod.module.json, the
documentation, evidence/ and presentation/thumbnail.svg. They are original
work. No code, constants or tables were taken from another reverb. The LCD
screenshots and media/capture.json are covered by media/LICENSE.md
(LicenseRef-OT-UI-Documentation), not by this licence.

The design follows Tom Erbe, "Building the Erbe-Verb: Extending the Feedback
Delay Network Reverb for Modular Synthesizer Use", Proceedings of the
International Computer Music Conference (ICMC) 2015, published under the
Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 licence. The paper is credited, not copied.

E-Verb is not affiliated with, endorsed by or supported by Make Noise or Tom
Erbe. Erbe-Verb is a product of Make Noise; the name is used only to describe
what this effect was modelled after.

The module is built by octabam's builder (sdk/octabam, MIT, Sam Banks; see
sdk/octabam/LICENSE and sdk/octabam/THIRD_PARTY.md), which is not part of this
folder. Nothing here contains or extends to Elektron Music Machines firmware,
which users supply from their own unit and which remains the property of its
copyright holder. Octatrack and Elektron are trademarks of Elektron Music
Machines MAV AB, used only to identify the hardware this module runs on.
